Hi Cristina,

Consider looking at https://github.com/shinra-dev/memuse. While this is not specific to distributed computing, you can get sizes of local objects. Then you control printing of the information from different ranks via comm.cat <http://comm.cat>() or comm.print().

Also, all other R memory use tools, like those described in http://adv-r.had.co.nz/memory.html, are available for local memory use reporting.

Regards,

George

